the operation to retake the tanker  happened shortly after 7pm  special forces commandos from the sbs ab  sailed onto the deck from helicopters  hovering above  supported by colleagues who scaled the  side of the ship  the seven hijackers were captured  without being harmed and the ship was  retaken  there would have been two merlin uh mark  fours there have been two wildcats  um and the operation basically is there  to isolate the ship  uh secure the upper deck to make sure  there is no reaction from on board  and then the um sbs um commandos will be  roped on board obviously covered by the  wildcats and  personnel in the helicopters they would  immediately  make sure the crew is safe and then  secure the stairways  uh wherever they are in the ship i think  the operation was all over  in seven minutes i hear from the time it  started  to the seven people being rounded up the  tanker had been stationary a few miles  off the coast of the isle of wight  for most of the day one of the world's  busiest shipping names  she was due to dock in southampton on  sunday morning but started steering  an erratic course shortly after 10 30 am  images from the marine traffic website  showed her zig zagging movement  for almost two hours the stairways began  acting violently when the crew  discovered them and tried to lock them  in a cabin  we don't know what the people on board  were trying to do perhaps they were  trying to threaten to run the ship  aground and  spill the oil of the cargo or perhaps to  try and do something even worse they  seem to come  from the new um center of piracy in the  world which is off  off the west african coast but whether  they were trying to sort of coerce  themselves into the uk which  strikes me a little odd or we're just  trying to sort of carry out some kind of  terrorist attack which perhaps is more  likely  it's hard to say the nave andromeda left  the nigerian port of lagos  on october the 6th it arrived in the  canary islands port of las palmas nine  days later  on october the 15th and left a few hours  later for southampton  it stopped a few miles out south of the  isle of wight  and an exclusion zone was established  and maritime coast guard helicopters  flew over it  for most of the day the flash to bang  as they say in the military was pretty  quick but  these waters the sbs's training ground  they're based just around the coast  in pool and they practice boarding  tankers cargo ships and ferries  on the english channel the whole time so  in that respect  this could not have been a more  convenient location  for an operation of this kind from the  military's point of view this was  textbook and the government will be  pleased it didn't have an ongoing  standoff  in the middle of the english channel a  tricky situation was dealt with  in under 12 hours
 

